<div id="recipe-13320-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-13320-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="13320"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-13320-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Mix olive oil, fresh lime juice, salt, and honey in a mason jar and shake vigorously. Set aside.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Greek-watermelon-salad-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Watermelon salad dressing and the ingredients in a bowl." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Greek-watermelon-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Greek-watermelon-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Greek-watermelon-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Greek-watermelon-salad-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Greek-watermelon-salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Greek-watermelon-salad.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-13320-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place watermelon cubes, sliced cucumber, fresh mint, and basil in a large salad bowl.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-13320-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Right before serving, drizzle the dressing over the salad. Give it a gentle toss being careful not to bruise or break the watermelon chunks.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/melon-feta-salad-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/melon-feta-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/melon-feta-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/melon-feta-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/melon-feta-salad-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/melon-feta-salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/melon-feta-salad.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-13320-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Sprinkle the feta cheese on top, taste for seasoning, and add more if necessary.  Alternatively, you can sprinkle it with a pinch of sea salt. Serve cold.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>

<div id="recipe-13320-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yields:</strong> This recipe yields about 8 cups of cucumber watermelon salad ideal for serving 4 adults. The nutritional information below is per serving.</li>
<li><b>Serve it chilled.</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> This salad is best when served cold. I like to keep each ingredient in the refrigerator before and after prepping. This way, all the salad is perfectly chill (and super refreshing) before serving.</span></li>
<li><b>Assemble at the last minute: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Toss all the ingredients with the dressing just before serving. This keeps the integrity and texture of the watermelon and cucumber intact.</span></li>
<li><b>Be gentle while tossing: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Use gentle hands to keep the delicate ingredients&rsquo; shape and structure.</span></li>
<li><b>Make Ahead: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Prepare all the ingredients and store them in separate containers. You can also make the dressing 3 days in advance and keep it in a mason jar in the fridge. Toss it all together just before serving.</span></li>
<li><b>Storage:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Leftover salad will keep fresh in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 2 days. However, be aware that the watermelon mixture will collect water as it sits. Drain, sprinkle salad with fresh herbs, and toss with a touch more of the honey lime dressing to bring it back to life before serving.</span></li>
</ul></div></div>
